@node emacsctl CLI
@chapter emacsctl CLI

@cindex emacsctl
@cindex cmacsctl
@cindex command-line control

@command{emacsctl} (also installed as @command{cmacsctl} --- the two
names behave identically) is a standalone command-line client that
controls a running cmacs the way @command{kubectl} controls a
cluster: resource-style commands, structured @option{-o json/yaml}
output for scripting, named contexts, live watch streams, an
interactive multi-language REPL, and ssh-tunnelled remote instances.

It is pure GNU89 C over GLib/GObject, talks to the editor through
the typed D-Bus interfaces (@pxref{D-Bus Service}), and links no
Emacs objects.  Build with @option{--with-cmacs-emacsctl}; the
binary lands at @file{src/emacsctl}.

This chapter is mirrored in @file{doc_org/cmacs/emacsctl/} --- the
Org files are the primary interactive reference and the two
directories must stay in sync (run @file{tools/sync-docs.sh}).

